{"Title":"Order relative to authorizing the joint committee on Health Care Financing to make an investigation and study of  certain current Senate documents relative to the health care financing","BillNumber":"S2748","DocketNumber":null,"GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"J24","Name":"Joint Committee on Health Care Financing","Type":2,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J24","ResponseDate":"2024-04-24T13:29:32.11"},"Cosponsors":[],"JointSponsor":null,"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/S2748/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Order","Pinslip":"April 25, 2024 -- The committee on Health Care Financing, to whom was referred the Senate Bills to address barriers to HIV prevention medication (Senate, No. 619); relative to emergency insulin access (Senate, No. 651); and to increase health insurance affordability for small business (Senate, No. 1899), reports the accompanying Order  (Senate, No. 2748).","DocumentText":"\tOrdered, That the committee on Health Care Financing be authorized and directed to make an investigation and study of certain current Senate documents numbered 619, 651, and 1899 relative to Health Care Financing.\r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[{"Action":"Study","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J24","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J24"},"Votes":[]},{"Action":"Discharge to Another Committee","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J40","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J40"},"Votes":[]}],"Amendments":[]}